      "review_state": "published",
      "description": "The Eriai Gate (from \u0389\u03c1\u03af\u03b1\u03b9 \u03c0\u03cd\u03bb\u03b1\u03b9, \"tombs gate\") was a modern invention, derived from a misreading of the Etymologicon Magnum sv. \u1f28\u03c1\u03af\u03b1\u03b9, which says that all Athenian gates were sometimes referred to as \u0389\u03c1\u03af\u03b1\u03b9, because corpses were carried through them to the necropoleis outside the city.",
